ster), the registered account no longer existed (/profile/user-1787845482842 renders 'User not found'), both authored threads and all posted replies disappeared (home list back to the original 8 seeded threads) and vote state reset. localStorage, sessionStorage and cookies are all empty — state is only kept in memory.\", \"evidence\": null}, {\"item_id\": \"CS-14\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Empty form, whitespace-only title+body (category=Technology), and title+body without category were all rejected with toast 'Please fill in all fields'; stayed on /new-thread and no thread was created (verified later thread list unchanged). Message is generic but does flag missing fields.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CS-17\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"Password not verified at login\", \"actual\": \"Signed in at /login with registered email different@example.com but deliberately wrong password 'wrongpass999'; app redirected to / and header showed 'New Thread / qa_tester1', i.e. a full logged-in session was created with an incorrect password.\", \"evidence\": null}, {\"item_id\": \"CS-22\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"Guest gets a blank dead-end page instead of a sign-in screen\", \"actual\": \"Logged out, no 'New Thread' entry point exists anywhere in the UI (header only shows Login/Register). Opening /new-thread as a guest renders a completely blank page — #root contains only the toast container, no header, no login form, no redirect (URL stays /new-thread after 2s). The user is never taken to a sign-in screen and cannot return to discussion creation.\", \"evidence\": null}, {\"item_id\": \"CT-16\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Trending list ordered 156,124,92,89,78,67,56,47,0,0 (descending by upvotes). Upvoting 'QA Zephyr testing checklist thread' (0→1) immediately moved it above 'QA vote ordering probe thread' (0), so ranking updates with voting.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CT-19\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"Displayed reply total does not match listed replies\", \"actual\": \"/thread/thread-1 header says '23 replies' (and list card says 23) but the detail view renders 'Replies (2)' with only 2 reply items. Seeded threads' totals are fabricated and inconsistent with actual reply content.\", \"evidence\": null}, {\"item_id\": \"CT-20\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"No stated recent time window; ranking is all-time\", \"actual\": \"'Trending Discussions' and 'Most Active Discussions' views show only the subtitle 'Join the conversation with our community' — no period is stated anywhere (no 'this week/24h' label). Both rank by lifetime totals: every listed item is a thread posted 'over 2 years ago', ordered by all-time votes/replies rather than interactions within a recent window.\", \"evidence\": null}, {\"item_id\": \"CT-21\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"Category and community counts are hard-coded and never update\", \"actual\": \"Sidebar shows Technology (243), General Discussion (156), Gaming (312) etc. while /category/tech actually lists 3 threads and /category/gaming 1. Community Stats reads 1,045 Threads / 4,823 Replies / 892 Members although the forum contains 10 threads and 6 users. After creating 2 threads, 5 replies and 1 new member, every one of these numbers stayed identical (e.g. Technology still 243, Threads still 1,045, Members still 892).\", \"evidence\": null}]}"
